.032, 4166.857, 3581.761, 3967.349]}}, "early": {}, "ladder": {"state": "COUNTERTREND BOUNCE", "label": "UNCONFIRMED TURN", "action": "HIGH-RISK \u00b7 NIMBLE ONLY", "dir": "caution", "score": -25, "why": "A daily bottoming setup is forming (swing low in, momentum turned up) \u2014 but the higher timeframes haven't confirmed it: the bigger picture is still bearish (weekly momentum negative; investor cycle overdue). This is an UNCONFIRMED TURN, not a confirmed buy. Weekly confirmation lags price, so this exact reading covers BOTH bounces that fail AND the first leg of a genuine new cycle \u2014 you can't tell which in real time, so treat it as a risk/size signal, not a direction call. Measured: weekly-unconfirmed bottoming setups held the low ~49% of the time vs ~68% once the weekly turns up.", "next": "Nimble traders only \u2014 small size, defined stop below 112400.0. Not an investment buy yet. What would upgrade it: weekly momentum turning up, a reclaim of the investor-cycle low, or the first daily cycle right-translating \u2014 add on confirmation, not ahead of it.", "weekly_ok": false, "regime": "bear", "regime_label": "BEARISH", "regime_why": "weekly momentum negative; investor cycle overdue", "regime_score": -2.5, "regime_line": "Bigger picture: BEARISH \u2014 weekly momentum negative; investor cycle overdue (investor cycle week 33 \u00b7 daily cycle day 70).", "summary_line": "Short-term (daily): unconfirmed turn. Bigger picture (counter-trend): bearish.", "points": ["Bigger picture is bearish (counter-trend for a daily long)", "Swing low printed (buyers rejected the low)", "Back above the 10-day average, and it's turning up", "Daily momentum just crossed up"], "entry": {"tag": "UNCONFIRMED \u2014 HIGH RISK", "tag_zh": "\u672a\u786e\u8ba4 \u2014 \u9ad8\u98ce\u9669", "urgency": "caution", "text": "An unconfirmed turn: a daily low is forming while the bigger picture is still bearish. Nimble traders only \u2014 small size, defined stop below 112400.0. Not an investment buy until the weekly confirms; most of these fail, a minority start a new cycle.", "text_zh": "\u672a\u786e\u8ba4\u8f6c\u5411\uff1a\u65e5\u7ebf\u4f4e\u70b9\u6b63\u5728\u5f62\u6210\uff0c\u4f46\u5927\u5c40\u4ecd\u504f\u7a7a\u3002\u4ec5\u9650\u7075\u6d3b\u4ea4\u6613\u8005\u2014\u2014\u5c0f\u4ed3\u4f4d\u3001\u6b62\u635f\u8bbe\u4e8e 112400.0 \u4e0b\u65b9\u3002\u5728\u5468\u7ebf\u786e\u8ba4\u524d\u5e76\u975e\u6295\u8d44\u6027\u4e70\u5165\uff1b\u591a\u6570\u6700\u7ec8\u5931\u8d25\uff0c\u5c11\u6570\u5219\u5f00\u542f\u65b0\u5468\u671f\u3002"}, "cycle_plain": {"daily_line": "Daily cycle: day 70 of a typical 36\u201342 trading days", "daily_phase": "overdue \u2014 past the typical window, so a low could form any day", "daily_line_zh": "\u65e5\u7ebf\u5468\u671f\uff1a\u7b2c 70 \u5929\uff0c\u5178\u578b\u5468\u671f\u4e3a 36\u201342 \u4e2a\u4ea4\u6613\u65e5", "daily_phase_zh": "\u903e\u671f\u2014\u2014\u5df2\u8d85\u8fc7\u5178\u578b\u7a97\u53e3\uff0c\u4f4e\u70b9\u968f\u65f6\u53ef\u80fd\u5f62\u6210", "weekly_line": "Weekly (investor) cycle: week 33 of a typical 16\u201326 weeks", "weekly_phase": "overdue \u2014 the bigger cycle is stretched, expect more volatility", "weekly_line_zh": "\u5468\u7ebf\uff08\u6295\u8d44\u8005\uff09\u5468\u671f\uff1a\u7b2c 33 \u5468\uff0c\u5178\u578b\u5468\u671f\u4e3a 16\u201326 \u5468", "weekly_phase_zh": "\u903e\u671f\u2014\u2014\u66f4\u5927\u7684\u5468\u671f\u5df2\u88ab\u62c9\u4f38\uff0c\u9884\u8ba1\u6ce2\u52a8\u52a0\u5267", "translation": "The last cycle peaked in its SECOND half ('right-translated') \u2014 strong cycles top late, a healthy-uptrend sign.", "translation_zh": "\u4e0a\u4e00\u5468\u671f\u5728\u540e\u534a\u6bb5\u89c1\u9876\uff08\u201c\u53f3\u79fb\u201d\uff09\u2014\u2014\u5f3a\u5468\u671f\u89c1\u9876\u504f\u665a\uff0c\u5c5e\u4e8e\u5065\u5eb7\u4e0a\u6da8\u8d8b\u52bf\u7684\u4fe1\u53f7\u3002"}, "early_note": "", "early_tier": null, "early_dir": null, "why_zh": "\u6b63\u5728\u5f62\u6210\u65e5\u7ebf\u7b51\u5e95\u5f62\u6001\uff08\u6446\u52